2026-01-30 14:32:20 | OUTPUT |     
2026-01-30 14:32:20 | OUTPUT |     Joke 2 is stronger in its delivery. The framing of China being "deeply disappointed" and then the spokesperson's internal monologue about democracy and freedom is genuinely funny. The self-deprecating humor implied in China questioning what Taiwan has that it doesn't is a clever twist. It's more unexpected and feels more naturally humorous than Joke 1's reliance on internet tropes. Joke 2 also feels more tightly written and avoids explaining itself. It commits fully to the bit. Both jokes are relevant to the headline, but Joke 2's punchline is more surprising and insightful.
